      <div type="clause" n="76.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 76.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="364" ed="#liebermann"/>Hit wæs ær þyson<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.7"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> cild, þe læg on<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.8"/> cradele, þeah hit næfre metes ne abite, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> þa gitseras<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.9"/> letan efen scyldig ⁊ hit gewittig wære.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="364" ed="#liebermann"/>Hit wæs ær ðysson, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> cild, ðe læg on ða<hi rend="italic">m</hi> cradole<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.4-2"/>, þeah hit næfre metes ne abite, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ða gytseras lætan ealswa scyldigne ⁊ hit gewittig wære.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.2" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="364" ed="#liebermann"/>Hit wæs ær þyssan, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> cild, þe læg on cradele, þeah hit næfre metes ne abite, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> þa gytseras leton efen scyldige ⁊ hit gewittig ware.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="76.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="365" ed="#liebermann"/>Fuit antea<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.5-2"/>, quod infans qui iacebat in cunabulis, licet numquam cibum gustasset, á githseris suis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.6-2"/> (rachinburgiis) putabatur ita (eque) reus, ác si intelligens esset.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="76.2" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="365" ed="#liebermann"/>Hactenus habita<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.4-3"/> est quędam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.5-3"/> praua<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.6-3"/> consuetudo in hac<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.7-2"/> terra, quia pueri qui iacebant in cunis, quanuis adhuc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.8-2"/> nullo cibo uterentur, iudicabantur ab auaris ęque rei, ac si scientiam haberent.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="76.2" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="365" ed="#liebermann"/>[76, 2] Ante hoc quidem consuetudo erat, quod etiam infantulum qui iacebat in cunis, licet nondum unquam comedisset, auari pariter reum (esse) decernebant, ac si intellectum haberet.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="76.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="214" ed="#robertson"/>Hit wæs ær ðysson þæt þæt cild ðe læg on ðam<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IICn_76-2.robnote.fn.6"/> cradole, þeah hit næfre metes ne abite, þæt ða gytseras lætan ealswa<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IICn_76-2.robnote.fn.7"/> scyldigne ⁊ hit gewittig wære.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="294" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Hit wæs ær þyson, þæt þæt cild þe læg on cradele, þeah hit næfre metes ne abite, þæt þa gitseras letan efen scyldig and hit gewittig wære.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="364" ed="#liebermann"/>Bisher galt es, dass das Kind<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.de.1"/>, welches in der Wiege<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.de.2"/> lag, auch wenn es [noch] nie Speise<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.de.3"/> gekostet hatte, dass dies die Habgierigen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.de.4"/> als ebenso schuldig behandelten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.de.5"/>, wie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_76-2.lnote.de.6"/> wenn es urtheilsfähig wäre.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Until now it was the case that the child that lay in the cradle, even if it had [yet] never tasted food, that the greedy treated it as just as guilty as if it were capable of understanding.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_76-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="215" ed="#robertson"/>It has been the custom up till now for grasping persons to treat a child which lay in the cradle, even though it had never tasted food, as being as guilty as though it were fully intelligent.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="473" ed="#whitelock"/>Up till now it happened that the child which lay in the cradle, although it had never tasted food, was reckoned by avaricious folk as being as guilty as though it had discretion.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="295" ed="#rabin-doml"/>It so happened before this that avaricious persons would treat a child in the cradle, even though it had never eaten solid food, as if it were guilty and complicit.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="364">Wulfstan p. 158</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. Wulfstan p. 158</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares Wulfstan p. 158.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 365, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">on cradele: on ðam cradele B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">letan efen scyldig: lætan ealswa scyldigne B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Antea qui. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Antea qui. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nunquam co. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nunquam co. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">comm. <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">comm. Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">364</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verbessert aus</hi> -len</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from -len</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ante bacum (<hi rend="italic">aus</hi> antehac?) <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ante bacum (from antehac?) K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">g. s. p. i. r. <hi rend="italic">K</hi>; ra. p. e. r. <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">g. s. p. i. r. K; ra. p. e. r. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">364</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þyssā <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þyssā Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">364</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þæm <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þæm added by Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">364</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gyt. leton e. scyldige <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gyt. leton e. scyldige Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.4-3" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">est h. <hi rend="italic">Lb Ct</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">est h. Lb Ct</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.5-3" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Rl Pl Ct</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Rl Pl Ct</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.6-3" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">c. p. <hi rend="italic">Lb Pl</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">c. p. Lb Pl</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">Anglia</hi> <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> h. t. <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Anglia</hi> instead of h. t. Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">am Rande Cb's Corrector</hi>; <hi rend="italic">fehlt Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in the margin by Cb's corrector; lacking in Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Kind 4. 7; mündig 4. 7—10a. Christian III. von Dänemark klagt 1537, das Wiegenkind zwinge man, zur Wergeldzahlung beizutragen; Phillpott <hi rend="italic">Kindred</hi> 82</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Kind 4. 7; mündig 4. 7—10a. Christian III of Denmark complains in 1537 that the child in the cradle is being compelled to contribute to the payment of wergild; Phillpott <hi rend="italic">Kindred</hi> 82</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das Wort <hi rend="italic">cradol</hi> heisst vielleicht ursprünglich nur ‘Kinderbett ohne Schaukelhölzer’; solches begegnet in Abbildungen; Stephani <hi rend="italic">Ält. dt. Wohnbau</hi> I 427. Und die Etymologie des Wortes deutet nicht (wie ‘Wiege’) auf Schaukeln, sondern auf Korb (Kluge <hi rend="italic">Etymol. Wb</hi>.). Allein mindestens seit 13. Jh. steht heutiger Sinn fest (Mätzner <hi rend="italic">Mengl. Wb</hi>. 497); und die Glossierung und Übs. durch <hi rend="italic">cunae, cunabula</hi>, dessen Sinn ‘Schaukelbett’ bekannt war, spricht dafür, dass die Agsa. dieses meinten</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The word <hi rend="italic">cradol</hi> perhaps originally meant only ‘child's bed without rockers’; such beds occur in illustrations; Stephani <hi rend="italic">Ält. dt. Wohnbau</hi> I 427. And the etymology of the word points not to rocking (as with ‘Wiege’) but to a basket (Kluge <hi rend="italic">Etymol. Wb</hi>.). But at least from the 13th cent. the present meaning is established (Mätzner <hi rend="italic">Mengl. Wb</hi>. 497); and the glossing and translation by <hi rend="italic">cunae, cunabula</hi>, whose meaning ‘rocking bed’ was known, suggests that the Anglo-Saxons meant this</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Kind 4. 7; mündig 4. 7—10a. Christian III. von Dänemark klagt 1537, das Wiegenkind zwinge man, zur Wergeldzahlung beizutragen; Phillpott <hi rend="italic">Kindred</hi> 82</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Kind 4. 7; mündig 4. 7—10a. Christian III of Denmark complains in 1537 that the child in the cradle is being compelled to contribute to the payment of wergild; Phillpott <hi rend="italic">Kindred</hi> 82</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Harte Gerichtsvögte, die es versklavten; Steenstrup <hi rend="italic">Danelag</hi> 107. 337.—Rachinburgen (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi>) missverstand Q</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Harsh judicial reeves who enslaved it; Steenstrup <hi rend="italic">Danelag</hi> 107. 337.—Q misunderstood it as Rachinburgen (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi>)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl</hi>. Toller <hi rend="italic">lætan</hi> 613b IV</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf</hi>. Toller <hi rend="italic">lætan</hi> 613b IV</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76-2.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zur Konstruktion <hi rend="italic">s. o</hi>. 51, 1³</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On the construction <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> 51, 1³</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_76-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. Wulfstan, p. 158, and the complaint made by Christian III of Denmark in 1537 (Phillpotts, <hi rend="italic">Kindred and Clan</hi>, p. 82).</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_76-2.robnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope></bibl><label>ðam</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. G, A.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_76-2.robnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope></bibl><label>ealswa</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">efen</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
